        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4c64c55b-6966-529e-b94f-049076ac8983",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Joseph Roth, Cid Corman\n- Roles: journalist, novelist, poet, translator, editor\n- Works: Juden auf Wanderschaft, Job, Radetzky March, Origin, The Wandering Jews\n- Topics: Austro-Hungarian Empire, Jewish life, Jewish migrations, American poetry\n\nFacts:\n- Joseph Roth was born Moses Joseph Roth on 2 September 1894 and died on 27 May 1939.\n- Joseph Roth was an Austrian-Jewish journalist and novelist.\n- Joseph Roth wrote the essay Juden auf Wanderschaft in 1927, and it was translated into English as The Wandering Jews.\n- Juden auf Wanderschaft gives a fragmented account of Jewish migrations from eastern to western Europe after World War I and the Russian Revolution.\n- Joseph Roth published the novel Job in 1930, and it is about Jewish life.\n- Joseph Roth published the family saga Radetzky March in 1932, and it is about the decline and fall of the Austro-Hungarian Empire.\n- Cid Corman was born Sidney Corman on 29 June 1924 and died on 12 March 2004.\n- Cid Corman was an American poet, translator, and editor.\n- Cid Corman was most notably the editor of Origin.\n- Cid Corman was a key figure in the history of American poetry in the second half of the 20th century.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a88c21c5-f01d-5245-988a-6e98ea54673b",
        "text": "Page: Joseph Roth. Sentence: Joseph Roth, born Moses Joseph Roth (2 September 1894 – 27 May 1939), was an Austrian-Jewish journalist and novelist, best known for his family saga \"Radetzky March\" (1932), about the decline and fall of the Austro-Hungarian Empire, his novel of Jewish life, \"Job\" (1930), and his seminal essay \"Juden auf Wanderschaft\" (1927; translated into English in \"The Wandering Jews\"), a fragmented account of the Jewish migrations from eastern to western Europe in the aftermath of World War I and the Russian Revolution.\nPage: Cid Corman. Sentence: Cid (Sidney) Corman (June 29, 1924 – March 12, 2004) was an American poet, translator and editor, most notably of \"Origin\", who was a key figure in the history of American poetry in the second half of the 20th century.",
